dia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Miraj_by_Sultan_Muhammad.jpg/500px-Miraj_by_Sultan_Muhammad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1543 illustration of Muhammad's Night Journey. His ascension to the heavens is often interpreted as an allegory for the human soul ascending to the celestial realms in Islamic philosophy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMiraj_by_Sultan_Muhammad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/4DModel.jpg/500px-4DModel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/4DModel.jpg/1280px-4DModel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/4DModel.jpg/500px-4DModel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A visual rendition of the Islamic model of the soul showing the position of nafs relative to other concepts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A4DModel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Muhammad_ibn_Muhammad_Shakir_Ruzmah-%27i_Nathani_-_A_Soul_Symbolized_as_an_Angel_-_Walters_W65944A_-_Full_Page.jpg/500px-Muhammad_ibn_Muhammad_Shakir_Ruzmah-%27i_Nathani_-_A_Soul_Symbolized_as_an_Angel_-_Walters_W65944A_-_Full_Page.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Muhammad_ibn_Muhammad_Shakir_Ruzmah-%27i_Nathani_-_A_Soul_Symbolized_as_an_Angel_-_Walters_W65944A_-_Full_Page.jpg/500px-Muhammad_ibn_Muhammad_Shakir_Ruzmah-%27i_Nathani_-_A_Soul_Symbolized_as_an_Angel_-_Walters_W65944A_-_Full_Page.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Muhammad ibn Muhammad Shakir Ruzmah-'i Nathani – A Soul Symbolized as an Angel (1717)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F